 the region of Persis, located in the southwestern part of the Iranian plateau, had been settled by Persian people."},{"qid":"Q63158027","from_t":1789,"to_t":1920,"method":"name-alias+date","confidence":0.8056507071215852,"label":"Qajar Iran","description":"country in Western Asia (1789–1925)","inception":1789,"dissolved":1925,"enwiki":"Qajar Iran","summary":"The Guarded Domains of Iran, commonly known as Qajar Iran, was the Iranian state under the rule of the Qajar dynasty, which lasted from 1789 to 1925. It was founded by Agha Mohammad Khan, a chieftain of the Qajar tribe, a Turkic tribe based in northern Iran. In the power struggle following the death of Karim Khan Zand in 1779, Agha Mohammad defeated all competitors from the preceding Zand and Afsharid dynasties, unifying Iran. He re-asserted Iranian sovereignty over large parts of the Caucasus and was formally crowned as Shah in 1796."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q83311","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q3616","value_label":"Tehran","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Tehran"},{"qid":"Q83311","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q794","value_label":"Iran","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Iran"},{"qid":"Q63158027","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q3616","value_label":"Tehran","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Tehran"},{"qid":"Q63158027","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q9168","value_label":"Persian","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Persian"},{"qid":"Q63158027","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q9168","value_label":"Persian","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Persian"},{"qid":"Q63158027","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q3449805","value_label":"South Azerbaijani","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"South Azerbaijani